#!/bin/bash
# Prints a release's notes: the one command that installs it, every reference it publishes under its version,
# and the versions the two zone images carry (images/versions).
# Usage: release/notes <tag or version>      Reads DOCKERHUB_NAMESPACE as release/references does.
set -euo pipefail
root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
refs=$("$root/release/references" "${1-}")
# The tag, whether the release was named by its tag or by its version.
tag=v${1#v}
# The references of one artifact, as a list.
listed() { awk -v a="$1" '$1 == a { print "- `" $2 "`" }' <<<"$refs"; }
cat <<OUT
## Install it

\`\`\`
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/toon-protocol/spaceturtle/$tag/install.sh | SPACETURTLE_VERSION=$tag bash
\`\`\`

It needs Linux on x86_64 with KVM, and no account anywhere. It installs the launcher of this release and starts nothing. Then:

\`\`\`
spaceturtle start     # about a minute after the first pull; makes the Install on devnet
spaceturtle key       # your model provider's key, read without showing it
spaceturtle           # talk to your agent
\`\`\`

An Install that is there already moves to this release with the same command, then \`spaceturtle upgrade\`.

## What this release publishes

The agent definition, an OCI artifact holding \`agent/spaceturtle.yaml\` byte for byte as the gate checked it:

$(listed definition)

The agent's zone image:

$(listed agent)

The connector's zone image:

$(listed connector)

## Versions in the images

\`\`\`
$("$root/images/versions")
\`\`\`
OUT
